{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumvertexcover()"]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is the complement of the lexicographically greatest maximum independent set, not of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least one: the least vertex of a symmetric difference is in one cover exactly when it is in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the other cover’s complement. That set is found as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":", with each choice the other way round: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"core pass on a bipartite component leaves out each vertex it decides, a complete component"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps its greatest vertex, and any other component deletes a vertex whenever a maximum set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without it remains, with the reductions taking a simplicial vertex greater than all its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neighbours. The cost is that of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":": O(m √n) on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bipartite components, and up to c exponential searches on a component of c vertices the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reductions do not settle. The search does not check for task cancellation."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first minimum vertex cover: of the smallest vertex covers, the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by vertex index (the rule of "},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": of two covers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of one size, the lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference), in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order; [] for the empty graph. Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"Covering","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"symbolKind":"method","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE40lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCoverSay0G0QzGyF","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1739","fileName":"ExactCovering.swift"},"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Co